{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Make one with the subject’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeSubscription()"},{"text":". It subscribes when it is made, exactly like the subject’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterator: a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CurrentValueSubject"},{"text":"’s subscription starts with the current value, and every value sent after that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is buffered for it, without limit, until ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","isActive":true},{"text":" returns it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The difference is cancellation. Cancelling a task waiting in an iterator’s "},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ends that iterator’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscription and discards its buffer. Cancelling a task waiting in a subscription’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" throws"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from that call only: the subscription stays subscribed, and a later "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values sent before and after the cancellation, in order. That suits a consumer that runs in rounds, such as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch run that is cancelled and started again, and must not miss what was sent between rounds."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The subscription unsubscribes when its last copy is released. It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncIteratorProtocol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operator can read it through ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence","type":"reference"},{"text":"; a cancelled read then ends that operator’s run with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and leaves the subscription for the next run.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","text":"Example","level":2},{"code":["let events = PassthroughSubject<String>()","let subscription = events.makeSubscription()","","let firstRound = Task { try await subscription.next() }","firstRound.cancel() \/\/ Throws CancellationError from that wait; nothing is lost.","_ = await firstRound.result","","events.send(\"launch\")","events.send(\"login\")","let first = try await subscription.next()  \/\/ \"launch\"","let second = try await subscription.next() \/\/ \"login\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wait on a subscription from one task at a time. Calling ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"text":" while another call on the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscription is still waiting traps.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/ScI"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A place in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject"},{"text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to, keeping every value sent in between.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"SubjectSubscription","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:7Afluent19SubjectSubscriptionV","modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubjectSubscription.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription.swift#L40"}},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementat